    "lastText": "I built `ledger` as described in `TASK.md`. All 8 tests pass with `npm test`.\n\nThe tests cover the commands end to end: validation, monthly repeat, filters, budgets, report, edit, delete, undo, import/export and `--help`. I did not run each README example by hand. Nothing has been committed.\n\n- **`bin/ledger.js`:** the CLI, with all the commands, `--file` accepted anywhere after the command, and exit codes of 2 for bad usage and 1 for `import` with invalid rows or `undo` with nothing to undo.\n- **`src/`:** the `Ledger` class plus the money, date and CSV helpers. Amounts are stored as integer cents, so adding `0.1` and `0.2` gives `0.30`.\n- **`test/ledger.test.js`:** the test suite.\n- **`README.md`:** every command with an example.\n\nTwo behaviours the spec left open:\n- **Undo history:** it is saved in the ledger file itself, under an `undo` key, so `undo` works across separate runs.\n- **Undo and IDs:** undoing an `add` does not rewind the id counter, so ids are never reused. The next `add` after an undo gets a new id, not the one that was undone.\n\nThe first attempt to write the files failed on a shell heredoc error, so I recreated them with the file-writing tool.",
